# Python FastAPI Best Practices — Clinic Service

### Project Overview
Product Context: I am building an AI-powered tele-dermatology and medicine fulfillment backend.

Workflow:
**User Submission:** Patient submits a questionnaire with skin/hair photos and videos.
**AI Diagnosis:** Backend runs inputs asynchronously through a local Vision-LLM (Ollama) to generate a diagnosis.
**Paywall:** User sees a blurred preview, pays a consultation fee to unlock full findings, and triggers a doctor review.
**Doctor Review:** Doctor gets notified (Push/SMS/WhatsApp) to Accept (customizes medicine kit), Reject (triggers auto-refund), or Request Info (user resubmits).
**Fulfillment:** Approved user pays for the kit => triggers third-party logistics API for delivery.

## Service Responsibility
This repository hosts the **Clinic Service**, which acts as the core clinical engine for the Skin & Hair Diagnosis app.
It owns and manages:
- **Questionnaires:** Template definitions, dynamic questions, image/video attachment metadata.
- **Questionnaire Submissions:** Patient response ingestion and payload preparation.
- **Diagnoses:** Asynchronous trigger to self-hosted LLM, partial/full diagnosis visibility rules, state tracking.
- **Consultations:** Routing cases to doctors, managing doctor actions (Accept, Reject, Request Info).
- **Prescriptions & Medicine Kits:** Doctor modification of treatment plans, custom kit assembly, and kit finalization.

